```Title: Service Control Manager Started a Shell or Script Host (raw Sysmon events)```
```ATT&CK: T1569.002 | Severity: high | Sigma id: e55e1c9b-bcf9-479e-bc4d-9bdb660bbab4```
```Data source: Sysmon EventCode 1 (Splunk Add-on for Sysmon). Change index to where your Sysmon data lives.```
```False positives: Services of backup and management products whose binary path is a script (review and allowlist)```
```Suggested ES correlation search: cron */15 * * * *, earliest=-20m@m latest=-5m@m, throttle on the table fields, notable severity high.```
index=sysmon source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
(ParentImage="*\\services.exe" Image IN ("*\\cmd.exe", "*\\powershell.exe", "*\\pwsh.exe", "*\\mshta.exe", "*\\wscript.exe", "*\\cscript.exe", "*\\rundll32.exe", "*\\regsvr32.exe"))
| table _time host User ParentImage Image CommandLine
